the delivery of an officer’s certificate by the other party certifying satisfaction of the three preceding conditions (and, in the case of Globalstar, the satisfaction of the conditions described in the following paragraph).", "location": "S-4/A, SUMMARY — Conditions to Completion of the Mergers, page 22", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "In addition, Amazon’s obligation to consummate the mergers is subject to the satisfaction or waiver of Globalstar’s receipt of certain governmental authorizations related to the C-3 system and their continuance in full force and effect and the achievement by Globalstar of certain milestones relating to the launch and operation of HIBLEO-4 replacement satellites.", "location": "S-4/A, SUMMARY — Conditions to Completion of the Mergers, page 22", "relevance_score": 5}], "event_status": [{"quote": "Amazon and Globalstar currently expect the mergers to be completed in 2027, subject to the satisfaction or waiver of the closing conditions contained in the merger agreement.", "location": "S-4/A, QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGERS, page 11", "relevance_score": 5}], "security_description": [{"quote": "In accordance with the Certificate of Designation of Perpetual Preferred Stock, Series A, $0.0001 par value per share, of Globalstar (the “Globalstar preferred stock” and such certificate of designation, “Globalstar’s Certificate of Designation”), at the effective time of the first merger, each share of Globalstar preferred stock outstanding will be automatically converted into the right to receive a liquidating distribution in the initial amount of the liquidation preference of $1,000 per share in cash plus any unpaid accrued dividends on such share.", "location": "S-4/A, QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGERS, page 10", "relevance_score": 5}], "effective_date": [], "available_options": [{"quote": "at the effective time of the first merger, each share of Globalstar preferred stock outstanding will be automatically converted into the right to receive a liquidating distribution in the initial amount of the liquidation preference of $1,000 per share in cash plus any unpaid accrued dividends on such share.", "location": "S-4/A, QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGERS, page 10", "relevance_score": 5}], "default_option": [], "election_deadline": [], "merger_subsidiary": [{"quote": "Grapefruit Acquisition Sub I, Inc., a direct, wholly owned subsidiary of Amazon (“Acquisition Sub I”), Grapefruit Acquisition Sub II, LLC, a direct, wholly owned subsidiary of Amazon (“Acquisition Sub II”)", "location": "S-4/A, QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGERS, page 1", "relevance_score": 5}], "cash_consideration_qualifications": [{"quote": "In accordance with Globalstar’s Certificate of Designation, at the effective time of the first merger, each share of Globalstar preferred stock outstanding will be automatically converted into the right to receive a liquidating distribution in the initial amount of the liquidation preference of $1,000 per share in cash plus any unpaid accrued dividends on such share.", "location": "S-4/A, THE MERGER AGREEMENT — Treatment of Globalstar Preferred Stock, page 103", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "Each party to the merger agreement and the exchange agent will be entitled to deduct and withhold from the merger consideration, the amount paid to holders of Globalstar preferred shares, and any amounts otherwise payable pursuant to the merger agreement to any person, such amounts as are required to be deducted and withheld under the Code or any other applicable tax law.", "location": "S-4/A, THE MERGER AGREEMENT — Withholding Rights, page 102", "relevance_score": 5}], "stock_exchange_ratio_type": [], "stock_exchange_ratio_qualifications": [], "other_consideration": [], "expected_closing": [{"quote": "Amazon and Globalstar currently expect the mergers to be completed in 2027, subject to the satisfaction or waiver of the closing conditions contained in the merger agreement.", "location": "S