{"acquirer": [{"quote": "If the Merger is completed, each share of common stock, par value $0.001 per share, of Sanara (“Sanara Common Stock”), excluding shares held by MiMedx, Sanara or their wholly-owned subsidiaries or shareholders who are entitled to demand and properly demand appraisal of such shares in accordance with Chapter 10, Subchapter H of the Texas Business Organizations Code (“TBOC”), that is issued and outstanding immediately prior to the effective time of the Merger (the “Effective Time”), will be canceled and converted into the right to receive (i) $33.00 in cash, without interest (the “Per Share Cash Consideration”) and (ii) 0.4735 shares of common stock (the “Per Share Stock Consideration”), par value $0.001 per share, of MiMedx (the “MiMedx Common Stock”) and, if applicable, cash in lieu of fractional shares, subject to adjustment as described in this proxy statement/prospectus and subject to applicable withholding taxes (the consideration described in the foregoing clauses (i) and (ii), collectively, the “Merger Consideration”).", "location": "PROPOSED MERGER — YOUR VOTE IS VERY IMPORTANT", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "On July 29, 2026, MiMedx Group, Inc., a Florida corporation (“MiMedx”), Mustang Merger Sub, Inc., a Texas corporation and wholly-owned subsidiary of MiMedx (“Merger Sub”), and Sanara MedTech Inc., a Texas corporation (“Sanara”), entered into an Agreement and Plan of Merger (as it may be amended from time to time, the “Merger Agreement”).", "location": "PROPOSED MERGER — YOUR VOTE IS VERY IMPORTANT", "relevance_score": 5}], "target": [{"quote": "On July 29, 2026, MiMedx Group, Inc., a Florida corporation (“MiMedx”), Mustang Merger Sub, Inc., a Texas corporation and wholly-owned subsidiary of MiMedx (“Merger Sub”), and Sanara MedTech Inc., a Texas corporation (“Sanara”), entered into an Agreement and Plan of Merger (as it may be amended from time to time, the “Merger Agreement”). Pursuant to the Merger Agreement, Merger Sub will merge with and into Sanara, with Sanara surviving and becoming a wholly-owned subsidiary of MiMedx (the “Merger”).", "location": "PROPOSED MERGER — YOUR VOTE IS VERY IMPORTANT", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "At the Effective Time, each share of Sanara Common Stock issued and outstanding immediately prior to the Effective Time, excluding shares held by MiMedx, Sanara or their wholly-owned subsidiaries or shareholders who are entitled to demand and properly demand appraisal of such shares in accordance with Chapter 10, Subchapter H of the TBOC will be automatically canceled and converted into the right to receive (x) $33.00 per share in cash, without interest, and (y) 0.4735 shares of MiMedx Common Stock.", "location": "THE MERGER — Merger Consideration, page 33", "relevance_score": 5}], "consideration_type": [{"quote": "At the Effective Time, each share of Sanara Common Stock issued and outstanding immediately prior to the Effective Time, excluding shares held by MiMedx, Sanara or their wholly-owned subsidiaries or shareholders who are entitled to demand and properly demand appraisal of such shares in accordance with Chapter 10, Subchapter H of the TBOC will be automatically canceled and converted into the right to receive (x) $33.00 per share in cash, without interest, and (y) 0.4735 shares of MiMedx Common Stock.", "location": "THE MERGER — Merger Consideration, page 33", "relevance_score": 5}], "cash_consideration": [{"quote": "Except as otherwise provided in Section 2.2(b) or Section 2.5, each share of Company Stock issued and outstanding immediately prior to the Effective Time (except for Company Stock to be canceled under Section 2.2(b) and Dissenting Shares) (each, a “Converted Share”) shall be converted into the right to receive (i) $33.00 in cash, without interest (the “Per Share Cash Consideration”), and (ii) 0.4735 shares of Parent Common Stock (the “Per Share Stock Consideration”, and together with the Per Share Cash Consideration, the “Merger Consideration”).", "location": "Annex A — Section 2.2(a) Conversion of Shares, page A-10", "relevance_score": 5}], "stock_exchange_ratio": [{"quote": "Except as otherwise provided in Section 2.2(b) or Section 2.5, each share of Company Stock issued and outstanding immediately prior to the Effective Time (except for Company Stock to be canceled under Section 2.2(b) and Dissenting Shares) (each, a “Converted Share”) shall be converted into the right to receive (i) $33.00 in cash, without interest (the “Per Share Cash Consideration”), and (ii) 0.4735 shares of Parent Common Stock (the “Per Share Stock Consideration”, and together with the Per Share Cash Consideration, the “Merger Consideration”).", "location": "Annex A — Section 2.2(a) Conversion of Shares, page A-10", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "references in this proxy statement/prospectus to “MiMedx Common Stock” refer to the common stock of MiMedx, par value $0.001 per share", "location": "QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE PROPOSED MERGER AND THE SPECIAL MEETING, page ii", "relevance_score": 5}], "shareholder_vote_date": [{"quote": "The Special Meeting will be held on September 30, 2026 at 9:00 a.m., Central Time. In order to facilitate shareholder attendance and participation, Sanara has determined that the Special Meeting will be held in a virtual meeting format only, via the Internet, with no physical in-person meeting. At the Special Meeting, Sanara’s shareholders will be asked to consider and vote on the Merger Proposal, the Advisory Compensation Proposal and the Adjournment Proposal.", "location": "SUMMARY — The Special Meeting, page 3", "relevance_score": 5}], "closing_conditions": [{"quote": "Each party’s obligations to effect the Merger are subject to the satisfaction or waiver (where permissible pursuant to applicable law) of the following conditions at or prior to the Closing:
• Sanara must have obtained the Sanara Shareholder Approval;
• no applicable law (whether temporary, preliminary or permanent) that restrains, enjoins or otherwise prohibits the consummation of the Merger may remain in effect;
• (i) any waiting period applicable to the Transactions must have expired or been terminated under the HSR Act, (ii) any commitment or agreement with any governmental authority in the United States to delay the Closing, or to not consummate the Transactions before a certain date, must have expired or terminated, and (iii) any approval, consent, registration, permit, authorization or other confirmation required to be obtained under antitrust laws must have been obtained or deemed obtained and remain in full force and effect;
• the Registration Statement must have been declared effective by the SEC under the Securities Act and no stop order suspending the Registration Statement must have been issued by the SEC; and
• the MiMedx Common Stock to be issued in connection with the Merger must have been approved for listing on Nasdaq, subject to official notice of issuance.", "location": "THE MERGER AGREEMENT — Conditions to the Closing of the Merger, page 83", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "In addition, the obligations of MiMedx and Merger Sub to effect the Merger are subject to the satisfaction or waiver (where permissible pursuant to applicable law) of the following conditions at or prior to the Closing:
• Sanara must have performed and complied in all material respects with all of its obligations under the Merger Agreement required to be performed or complied with by it at or prior to the Effective Time;", "location": "SUMMARY — Conditions to the Consummation of the Merger, page 9", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "• each of the representations and warranties of Sanara contained in the Merger Agreement regarding certain aspects of the capitalization of Sanara (as set forth in specified sections of the Merger Agreement) must have been true and correct in all respects at and as of the date of the Merger Agreement and must be true and correct in all respects at and as of the Closing (other than representations and warranties that by their terms address matters only as of another specified time, which must have been true as of such time), other than de minimis inaccuracies in representations and warranties of Sanara regarding its outstanding shares of stock and other outstanding securities;", "location": "SUMMARY — Conditions to the Consummation of the Merger, page 9", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "• since the date of the Merger Agreement, there must not have been a Material Adverse Effect (as defined in the section entitled “The Merger Agreement — Representations and Warranties”); and
• MiMedx must have received a certificate signed by an executive officer of Sanara certifying that the conditions described in the foregoing bullets have been satisfied.", "location": "SUMMARY — Conditions to the Consummation of the Merger, page 9", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "In addition, the obligations of Sanara to effect the Merger are subject to the satisfaction or waiver (where permissible pursuant to applicable law) of the following conditions:
• each of MiMedx and Merger Sub must have performed and complied in all material respects with all of its obligations under the Merger Agreement required to be performed by it at or prior to the Effective Time;", "location": "SUMMARY — Conditions to the Consummation of the Merger, page 9", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "• each of the other representations and warranties of MiMedx contained in the Merger Agreement (disregarding all materiality and MiMedx Material Adverse Effect qualifications contained therein) must have been true and correct at and as of the date of the Merger Agreement and must be true and correct at and as of the Closing (other than representations and warranties that by their terms address matters only as of another specified time, which must have been true as of such time), except for any failures of such representations and warranties to be true and correct as have not had and would not reasonably be expected to have, individually or in the aggregate, a MiMedx Material Adverse Effect (as defined in the section entitled “The Merger Agreement — Representations and Warranties”); and
• Sanara must have received a certificate signed by an executive officer of MiMedx, certifying that the conditions described in the foregoing bullets have been satisfied.", "location": "SUMMARY — Conditions to the Consummation of the Merger, pages 9–10", "relevance_score": 5}], "event_status": [{"quote": "We expect to complete the Merger in the fourth quarter of 2026. However, we cannot assure you of when or if the Merger will be completed. We must first obtain the approval of the Merger Proposal from Sanara’s shareholders, as well as obtain necessary regulatory approvals and satisfy certain other closing conditions.", "location": "QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE PROPOSED MERGER AND THE SPECIAL MEETING, page iv", "relevance_score": 5}], "security_description": [{"quote": "“Company Stock” means the Common Stock, par value $0.001 per share, of the Company.", "location": "Annex A — Section 1.1 Definitions, page A-3", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "each share of common stock, par value $0.001 per share, of Sanara (“Sanara Common Stock”)", "location": "PROPOSED MERGER — YOUR VOTE IS VERY IMPORTANT", "relevance_score": 5}], "effective_date": [], "available_options": [{"quote": "Except as otherwise provided in Section 2.2(b) or Section 2.5, each share of Company Stock issued and outstanding immediately prior to the Effective Time (except for Company Stock to be canceled under Section 2.2(b) and Dissenting Shares) (each, a “Converted Share”) shall be converted into the right to receive (i) $33.00 in cash, without interest (the “Per Share Cash Consideration”), and (ii) 0.4735 shares of Parent Common Stock (the “Per Share Stock Consideration”, and together with the Per Share Cash Consideration, the “Merger Consideration”).", "location": "Annex A — Section 2.2(a) Conversion of Shares, page A-10", "relevance_score": 5}], "default_option": [], "election_deadline": [], "merger_subsidiary": [{"quote": "On July 29, 2026, MiMedx Group, Inc., a Florida corporation (“MiMedx”), Must